! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F210 "STORE ROUNDED TEST
! ROUTINE", sub-test A5 (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.110, octal
! 016032.00-016041.40, where the routine's "TEST NORMALIZATION
! MODIFIER" section and F210A6 begin). Eleven rows, and it closes out
! F210A "ARITHMETIC CHECKS".
!
! A5 is the UNFLAGGED analogue of A1, and it asks the one thing about
! SRD that no sub-test so far has:
!
!   DL(U) FPK32 -- exponent +2, fraction all ones -- then C0011 drops
!   FPK32's all-ones fraction into the low half as well, so the
!   accumulator fraction is 96 ONES in the N range. SRD(U) rounds: the
!   +1 at IBM 60 carries the whole way out, the 96-bit sum is 2^47-1
!   with its high 48 bits zero, and there is an overflow bit.
!
!   Expected result FPK67 -- exponent STILL +2, fraction ZERO.
!
! That is the unnormalized overflow rule: "the overflow bit does not
! enter storage but sets the lost carry indicator (LC) on" (p.96). The
! exponent is NOT bumped to absorb it. A1 and A2 cannot check this
! because they are flagged, where the exponent is left alone by a
! different rule entirely; A3 and A4 cannot, because neither overflows
! out of the kept 48 bits. A5 is the first and only place the
! unnormalized overflow meets an exponent that WOULD move if the model
! treated the carry the way a normalized operation does.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant.
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pools pp.176-177. PASS sits at 016041.40, where F210A6 begins.
!
! Instructions: B, DL(U), C0011, SRD(U), L, CT0110, SIC, BZB, BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f210a5_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: passed on the first run, and an injection confirms it is
! the sole guard for that rule. Absorbing the unnormalized overflow
! into the exponent -- adding (ovf == 1 ? 1 : 0) alongside the
! normalization adjustment -- halts A5 with SIC storing 016037.40, the
! address right after its BRGZ, while F210A1-A2 and F210A3-A4 both
! stay green. Nothing else in the suite watches it, exactly as the
! reasoning above predicted.
!
! Still NOT covered by anything in F210A: the lost carry indicator
! itself. A5 produces the overflow that sets LC and never asks about
! it -- there is no BLC or BZLC anywhere in A1-A5. The routine's "TEST
! NORMALIZATION MODIFIER" section from 016041.40 is the next place
! that could.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pools pp.176-177) --
        SLC, (8)022045.0
FPK32   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022107.0
FPK67   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001000000000000000000

! The listing prints no label at 016032.00 -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand.
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)16032.0
ENTRY   B, $+.32                               ! F210A5: exponent of acc. operand in N range
        DL(U), FPK32
        C0011(BU,48), FPK32+.12, 20
        SRD(U), ROS                            ! adds 1 in bit position 60 of fraction
        L(BU), FPK67
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                  ! test result exp + +2, fract + 0 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, ROS+.60, $+2.0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                                 ! 016041.40: where F210A6 begins
        END, ENTRY
